<v Ira Glass>We spend a lot of time staring at this spreadsheet that came with Toxie. It lists all the mortgages, 2,000 of them, and financial data about the loans, but it doesn't give us what we need-- addresses and names. It just has zip codes. It's sort of like this map that you can't quite read.
<v Ira Glass>我们花了很多时间盯着这份随托克茜一起提供的电子表格。它列出了所有的抵押贷款，共计2000笔，以及关于这些贷款的财务数据，但它没有提供我们需要的东西——地址和姓名。它只有邮政编码。这有点像一张你根本看不懂的地图。

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:56.380
<v David Kestenbaum>So in the spring, we call an investigative reporter to help us find some of the people in the spreadsheet. Michael Braga with the Sarasota Herald Tribune in Florida. Sarasota, the very city that popped up over and over again when Wit showed us the loans and Toxie on his computer screen. So Michael went through public records databases, took him about a day, and he came up with nine names.
<v David Kestenbaum>所以在春天，我们打电话给一位调查记者，帮我们在电子表格里找到其中的一些人。迈克尔·布拉加（Michael Braga），来自佛罗里达州的《萨拉索塔先驱论坛报》。萨拉索塔，正是当威特在电脑屏幕上向我们展示贷款和托克茜时，一次又一次弹出的那个城市。所以迈克尔查阅了公共记录数据库，花了他大约一天时间，他找出了九个名字。

